Vendored third-party code
=========================

This directory contains a vendored copy of the NanoTabICLv2 *prior* (the TabICLv2
data-generating process) from:

    Project:  nanotabicl (a minimal TabICLv2 implementation)
    Source:   https://github.com/soda-inria/nanotabicl
    File:     prior.py
    Commit:   ead24e3a1bf2dcda3ec46041a5189c034b6c0a62
    sha256:   b64bb260feef0841151178272d5921703c7286e498f92e1654d992fb501c13f3
    License:  BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE in this directory)
    Copyright (c) 2025, Soda team @ Inria

Upstream describes it as a slightly simplified TabICLv2 prior that "performs similarly
well" to the full one. The sha256 above is of the file as fetched, before the edits below.

Modifications relative to upstream `prior.py`
---------------------------------------------
The generator's behaviour is unchanged — same mechanisms, same distributions, same
sampled constants. `prior.py` participates in the normal pre-commit hooks (black, ruff,
ty) rather than being excluded, so it conforms to the project like any other module:

- annotated the `node_values` placeholder list as `list[Any]` (it holds `None` until each
  node is filled in topological order, which `ty` cannot see through);
- removed the upstream `if __name__ == '__main__'` matplotlib plotting demo, which also
  drops a matplotlib import from a core-dependency module.

Behavioural divergence, opt-in only
-----------------------------------
An optional `eta: MechanismEta | None` threads through the eight functions on the path
to a family draw (`rand_dataset_filtered`, `rand_dataset_plain`, `rand_node_func`,
`rand_converter`, `rand_multi_func`, `rand_func`, `rand_prod_func`, `rand_points`). It
replaces upstream's uniform choice over the eight mechanism families with a grouped
simplex, split by role -- `rand_points` draws under the root-marginal simplex, every
other site under the mechanism simplex. See `mechanisms.py`.

`eta=None` is the default everywhere and takes upstream's own `randchoice` branch, so
the unmodified path is bit-identical, not merely equal in distribution; a test in
`tests/priors/test_mechanisms.py` pins that. At the origin eta the induced per-family
probability is exactly 1/8 (1/5 under `only_cheap`), so a tuned run has an exact null.

`rand_dataset_filtered` also gained `max_attempts` (default `None` = upstream's
unbounded retry). Corner etas can make most draws fail the ExtraTrees learnability
check, where an unbounded loop is indistinguishable from a hang.

It further rejects regression targets whose spread is below float32 resolution at their
own offset. Upstream's learnability check cannot reject a constant target: it compares
`(y - mean)**2` against `(y - oob)**2` in float32, and for a constant `y` the rounding
error of the mean makes the first term strictly positive while the trees reproduce `y`
exactly, so `pval` comes out `0.0` and a task carrying no signal is accepted as
learnable. Measured at roughly 0.25% of draws, and not eta-specific -- it fires on
upstream's own uniform mixture too. This is the one modification that changes which
draws upstream would have returned; the family draws themselves are untouched.

`tasks.py` in this directory is **ebpfn code, not vendored** — it adapts the upstream
generator to ebpfn's task contracts (exact `CharacterizationShape`, `TuningTask`,
deterministic seeding through `RandomStreams`).

Why vendored
------------
nanotabicl is not published to PyPI, so the generator is copied in rather than depended
on. It is here to answer one question: measured at equal training budget on the same
frozen backbone, does the TabICLv2 prior produce a better model than ebpfn's own
generator? Our own generator covers real-corpus property ranges poorly (feature skew
covers 1 of 9 real datasets; 2% of tasks are near-deterministic against 33% in real
data), which this arm is meant to confirm or refute.

If it wins, the mechanism library gets reimplemented against ebpfn's contracts with
tunable coordinates and this vendored copy is deleted; if it does not, the copy is
deleted and the completeness argument was wrong. Either way this directory is temporary.

Relationship to `ebpfn/pfn/nanotabicl/`
---------------------------------------
That directory vendors the *model* from the same upstream commit. Its NOTICE previously
stated that `prior.py` was deliberately not vendored; that statement is superseded here.
